 # CODEX_EXECUTION_REPORT
 
+## 2026-05-19 Phase 1 task_packet scope separation patch
+
+This pass is a Phase 1 small patch only. It does not advance the `samplereverse` reverse-engineering mainline, does not enter Phase 2, and does not implement Phase 1B/1C/1E/1F.
+
+### Audit Result
+
+| check | result |
+|---|---|
+| `build_task_packet()` task derivation | It reads `current_state["current_bottleneck"]` and calls `_task_from_bottleneck(current_state)` when model context is sufficient; when evidence is missing it emits `collect_missing_evidence`. |
+| meaning of `task_packet.task` | The field is derived from sample artifacts and model-gate state. It is not the current Codex execution task when `decision_packet.md` is an architecture handoff. |
+| active execution entry | `project_state/decision_packet.md` remains the current Codex execution authority. |
+| compatibility | The old `task` field is preserved unchanged, and the new fields are additive, so existing readers can keep using `task`. |
+| status output | `status_summary()` and CLI `status` now expose the task source and active decision packet so the command line distinguishes derived sample state from current execution scope. |
+
+### Changes Made
+
+- Added task scope fields to every `build_task_packet()` output: `state_scope`, `task_source`, `derived_task`, `active_decision_packet`, and `execution_scope`.
+- Kept `task` and `expected_gpt_output` for compatibility with existing GPT/Codex workflows.
+- Added tests covering `derived_task == task`, fixed source/scope values, active decision packet, and CLI/status visibility.
+- Phase 1B/1C/1E/1F remain unimplemented.
+
+### Verification This Round
+
+| command | result |
+|---|---|
+| `python -m py_compile reverse_agent\project_state.py` | passed |
+| `python -m pytest -q tests\test_project_state.py` | `48 passed in 7.19s` |
+| `python -m reverse_agent.project_state build --reports-dir solve_reports --sample samplereverse --run-name sr_lhs_last_writer_health_fix_20260518_r3` | passed; generated `round_20260519_041029` / `state_20260519_041029_d8b41081b53f` |
+| `python -m reverse_agent.project_state status` | `reason: instrumentation_incomplete`, `task_source: derived_from_sample_artifacts`, `active_decision_packet: project_state/decision_packet.md`, `missing: []` |
+| `python -m reverse_agent.project_state archive-round` | run after this report and `project_state/pytest_result.txt` are written so the archived round captures the final state files |
+
+### State Notes
+
+- `project_state/task_packet.json` still reports `task: Improve compare lhs last-writer instrumentation`, but now also reports that it is a derived sample-artifact task.
+- `project_state/decision_packet.md` remains the active task authority for Codex execution.
+- No artifact scanner, reverse strategy, runtime probe, beam, budget, frontier, or Base64/RC4 probe behavior changed.
+
